       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
